:true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":true,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_Catton\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://electricliterature.com/7-contemporary-novels-about-the-victorian-era/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.timesnownews.com/lifestyle/books/features/12-historical-fiction-books-that-bring-the-victorian-era-to-life-article-111604949\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\"\",\"title\":\"https://www.penguin.co.uk/discover/articles/books-that-defined-the-2010s\"}],\"next_step\":\"Open a received ref with read; use replay=true to restore full cached navigation.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":8,\"prior_deliveries\":2,\"query_key\":\"61705ead24e9e6dfb13e9ec8f70961b1d03ae1a342b6f2b042445b26da5e847e\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"d5d8785cacfed45349c77999689441cc64905be4d17cb01b48f25d6749e02962\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The Luminaries Eleanor Catton translated languages\",\"view\":\"reuse\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_ca3b8795bb05404f90e5ad29"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure more carefully. The award was created in the 2000s. Let me think about other awards created in the 2000s and look at the International Booker Prize Wikipedia page directly.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize Wikipedia\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_f6bfa661f5284b2aaf6e45b7","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"literary award founded 2004 2005 2006 2007 2008 2009 translated languages\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_5da898f1d5ac476d8a32f4c2","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... A sister prize, the International Booker Prize, is awarded for a work of fiction translated into English and published in the United Kingdom or Ireland. Unlike the Booker Prize, short story collections are eligible for the International Booker Prize. The £50,000 prize money is split evenly between ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... at the International Institute of Modern Letters. Her award-winning debut novel, The Rehearsal, written as her Master's thesis, was published in 2008, and has been adapted into a 2016 film of the same name. Her second novel, The Luminaries, won the 2013 Booker Prize, making Catton ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_Catton\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... It won the 2019 Pulitzer Prize for Fiction, was shortlisted for the Booker Prize and the $75,000 2019 PEN/Jean Stein Book Award, and was runner-up for the Dayton Literary Peace Prize.\\n\\nBewilderment, published in September 2021, was shortlisted for the 2021 Booker Prize and longlisted ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Powers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... If you want to understand modern-day Britain, this is the writer to read.\\\"\\n\\nAccolades\\n\\nGirl, Woman, Other was joint winner (with Margaret Atwood's The Testaments) of the 2019 Booker Prize,Flood, Alison (14 October 2019), \\\"Margaret Atwood and Bernardine Evaristo share Booker prize 2019\\\", The Guardian ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl,_Woman,_Other\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... The decade—and the Australian phase of Carey's career—culminated with the publication of Oscar and Lucinda (1988), which won the Booker McConnell Prize (as it was then known) and brought the author international recognition. Carey explained that the novel was inspired, in part, by his time ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Carey_(novelist)\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"6c7dbea58c810f25fc6d61078c627b96ebd24e6a9f2840b1366a93823e7379ce\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"a929d17558455f50bde956e80d1f2197f3e7a8e7d04ea1a8fd2241a07a4c4596\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":